      "question": "What are the AMA guidelines for A1C?",
      "type": "featured_snippet",
      "snippet": "The goal for most adults with diabetes is an A1C that is less than 7%. If your A1C level is between 5.7 and less than 6.5%, your levels have been in the prediabetes range. If you have an A1C level of 6.5% or higher, your levels were in the diabetes range.",
