    {
      "question": "What are the new guidelines for diabetes?",
      "type": "ai_overview",
      "text_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "snippet": "The 2025 American Diabetes Association (ADA) Standards of Care in Diabetes includes several key updates, including expanded guidance on continuous glucose monitor (CGM) use, medication management during shortages, and the use of GLP-1 receptor agonists for heart and kidney health. The document also emphasizes personalized care, including individual risk assessments for pre-diabetes and tailored approaches to weight management and obesity treatment.",
          "snippet_highlighted_words": [
            "expanded guidance on continuous glucose monitor (CGM) use, medication management during shortages, and the use of GLP-1 receptor agonists for heart and kidney health"
          ],
          "reference_indexes": [
            0,
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "snippet": "Here's a more detailed breakdown of the new guidelines:"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "1. CGM Use and Medication Management:",
          "reference_indexes": [
            6
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "title": "Continuous Glucose Monitors (CGMs):",
              "snippet": "The 2025 standards encourage the use of CGMs for adults with type 2 diabetes who are on glucose-lowering medications other than insulin."
            },
            {
              "title": "Medication Shortages:",
              "snippet": "New guidance addresses how to manage situations where medications are unavailable due to shortages, offering strategies for patients and providers.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "2. GLP-1 Receptor Agonists:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "title": "Beyond Weight Loss:",
              "snippet": "The updated guidelines highlight the benefits of GLP-1 receptor agonists for heart and kidney health, in addition to their established role in weight management."
            },
            {
              "title": "Sustained Weight Management:",
              "snippet": "The guidelines also address the continuation of weight management pharmacotherapy even after weight loss goals have been achieved.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                2
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "3. Personalized Care and Risk Assessment:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "title": "Individualized Risk/Benefit Assessment:",
              "snippet": "The importance of assessing individual risk and benefit when considering treatment options, particularly for pre-diabetes, is emphasized."
            },
            {
              "title": "Intensive Lifestyle Changes:",
              "snippet": "The guidelines recommend intensive lifestyle behavior changes for all individuals with overweight or obesity who are at risk for diabetes."
            },
            {
              "title": "Weight Management Goals:",
              "snippet": "The updated standards include specific goals for weight loss or prevention of weight gain, with a focus on cardiovascular risk factors."
            },
            {
              "title": "Local DPP Programs:",
              "snippet": "Referral to local Diabetes Prevention Programs (DPP) is also recommended.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                3
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "snippet": "4. Other Notable Updates:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "list": [
            {
              "snippet": "Sleep Health: Sleep is now recognized as a central component of diabetes management, alongside eating patterns and physical activity.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                3
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Vitamin D: The use of Vitamin D to prevent type 2 diabetes is discussed.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                3
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Cognitive Impairment: The standards include recommendations for monitoring cognitive capacity and referring patients for formal assessment if needed.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                5
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Bone Health: There is a new emphasis on evaluating and treating bone health in people with diabetes, including specific risk factors for fractures.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                1
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Screening for Metabolic Dysfunction-Associated Steatotic Liver Disease (MASLD): The guidelines recommend screening for MASLD in people with diabetes.",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0,
                1
              ]
            },
            {
              "snippet": "Recreational Cannabis: The use of recreational cannabis is discussed, with specific guidance for those with type 1 diabetes or those with other forms of diabetes at risk for diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA).",
              "reference_indexes": [
                0
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
